<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks fall.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks fall.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			24/7/97		  17/7/97	     26/7/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    400		  425-450	     350-375</p>
<p>    Naphtha	     100			100		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,800-1,825		    1,900	 1,400-1,425</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    275		  325-350	     450-475</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15			 15		    25</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks dipped as product left by barge and by cargo, including to the United States.</p>
<p>Naphtha inventories barely changed with steady in and out movements.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks dipped as a single cargo arrived, but material still left down the Rhine, including IPE-related product bound for Germany.</p>
<p>Fuel oil inventories fell as little product arrived and the bunker sector withdrew cracked material.</p>
<p>Jet fuel levels were steady with a little moving to the aviation sector.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
